  "result": "Perfect! All 193 tests pass (183 original + 10 new). I've successfully added payment terms support.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **Added error code** to `src/errors.js`:\n   - `TERMS_INVALID`: Payment terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM\n\n2. **Created `calculateDueDate()` helper** in `src/invoices.js`:\n   - **NET14**: Issue date + 14 days\n   - **NET30**: Issue date + 30 days (default)\n   - **EOM**: Last day of the issue month\n     - Handles month boundaries (Oct 15 \u2192 Oct 31)\n     - Handles year boundaries (Dec 15 \u2192 Dec 31)\n     - Handles leap years (Feb 15 in leap year \u2192 Feb 29)\n\n3. **Updated `createInvoice()`**:\n   - Accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to `'NET30'`)\n   - Validates terms and calculates due date\n   - Returns `TERMS_INVALID` error for invalid terms\n   - Stores both `terms` and `dueDate` on the invoice\n\n**Tests added (10 new):**\n- Default NET30 terms calculation\n- NET14 terms calculation\n- NET30 terms calculation\n- EOM on mid-month dates\n- EOM at end of month (same day as issue)\n- EOM at start of month (full month span)\n- EOM in non-leap February (ends on 28th)\n- EOM in leap February (ends on 29th)\n- EOM at year boundary (December \u2192 Dec 31)\n- Invalid terms rejection\n\nAll 193 tests pass, verifying payment terms are correctly calculated and stored with invoices.",
